  "limitations": [
    "The candidate still has a 0.7.3 development package revision; this is not the final 0.7.3-to-0.8.0 transition.",
    "The VM had no audio interface; the real user unit ran a signal receiver, not mixer code.",
    "All six corrected cycles had fresh kernel deep-entry/exit events. Only the first lasted about six seconds; later virtual-RTC wakes were immediate. This qualifies trigger ordering, not extended sleep or hardware state retention.",
    "Hibernate, hybrid sleep and suspend-then-hibernate were not exercised; their ordering is covered by software checks only.",
    "Other systemd distributions, NixOS resume and final-candidate hardware checks remain open.",
    "A subsequent isolated RPM fault probe found premature fence removal when systemctl daemon-reload fails. Its correction and native regression are separate from this successful-VM record."
